 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S443-003\", \"clauses\": {\"measure\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F09\", \"template\": \"How long is the object? Give your answer in {unit_name}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 asks the learner to find how long the object is and give the answer in a unit, which is measuring the length of an object.\"}, \"compare\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"{upper}{v} is {val_a} {unit} long. {upper2}{v2} is {val_b} {unit} long. Which length is {comp_word} in {unit}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 gives two object lengths in one unit and asks which length is longer or shorter, which is comparing lengths.\"}, \"lengths\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"{upper}{v} is {val_a} {unit} long. {upper2}{v2} is {val_b} {unit} long. Which length is {comp_word} in {unit}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 states the length of each object and asks the learner to compare those lengths.\"}, \"objects\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"{upper}{v} is {val_a} {unit} long. {upper2}{v2} is {val_b} {unit} long. Which length is {comp_word} in {unit}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 names objects from the pool (book, crayon, notebook, pencil, ruler, shoe, spoon) whose lengths are given and compared.\"}, \"meters_or_centimeters\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F03\", \"template\": \"The distance from the bench to the tree is {val_a} m. The distance from the gate to the tree is {val_b} m. Which distance is {comp_word} in meters?\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 expresses the measurements in meters; F07 expresses them in centimeters, so both named units are producible.\"}, \"distance\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F03\", \"template\": \"The distance from the bench to the tree is {val_a} m. The distance from the gate to the tree is {val_b} m. Which distance is {comp_word} in meters?\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 gives two distances in meters and asks which is longer or shorter.\"}, \"measuring_tools\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"Read the measurement on the ruler carefully.\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 directs the learner to read a measurement on a ruler, which is a measuring tool.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F01\", \"F06\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Compare {val_a} {count_noun} and {val_b} {count_noun2}.\", \"{max} is more than {min}.\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F01 draws count_noun and count_noun2 independently from the two-member list 'centimeter (cm)' and 'meter (m)', and its domain shows no link that forces both units to match, so a hint can compare a value in one unit with a value in the other. The competency names both units and comparing lengths, but it does not name converting or comparing across units, so a mixed-unit comparison asks for a skill outside the named scope and can mislead a learner who compares the bare numbers. The count_noun slots also print only singular unit words, so a plural value is printed with a singular unit word, which is ungrammatical. F06 prints two bare numbers with no unit, drawn from the two compared values. When those values carry different units, which F01 shows can happen, the statement that the first number is more than the second is false about the lengths. Not failed: F02 uses 'measurement', which is absent from cumulative_vocab but not in NOT_YET_KNOWN. F03 has no distinct flag on val_a and val_b, so the packet does not show whether they can be equal; this is noted, not a failure on its own. F04 and F05 print the answer inside hints, which is a design concern but not a Rule 1 fault.\"}",
